"""
progedit - A zero-dependency, nano-style terminal editor for programmers.
Forked from txtedit; works on macOS (Darwin), Ubuntu, RedHat/RHEL and other UNIX systems.

- Syntax highlighting for Python, Ruby, C and C++ (multi-line strings, comments,
  heredocs and preprocessor lines included), 10 colour themes (^T).
- Automatic indentation: keeps the indent, adds a level after ':' / '{' / Ruby block
  openers, re-aligns 'else' / 'end' / 'except' / '}', soft tabs, smart backspace.
- Language Server Protocol client (talks to pylsp / pyright / clangd / ruby-lsp /
  solargraph ... if installed): live diagnostics, completion, hover, go-to-definition.
- ^B / F5 compiles (C, C++) and runs the file in the terminal (also Python, Ruby).
- Soft word-wrap, search / replace (case + regex toggles), undo/redo, line cut/paste,
  go-to-line, bracket matching, bracketed-paste support, live line/word/char count.
"""

